  "title": "Squared Readings In Order",
  "description": "## Task\n\nA gauge reports signed offsets from a baseline, listed in sorted order. Produce the squares of all offsets, sorted in non-decreasing order, by scanning from both ends instead of sorting the squares.\n\n## Input\n\n- `offsets` — a list of integers sorted in non-decreasing order. It may be empty.\n\n## Output\n\nA list of the squares of the entries, sorted in non-decreasing order.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\nsquared_in_order([-4, -1, 0, 3, 10])  # returns [0, 1, 9, 16, 100]\nsquared_in_order([-3, -3, 2])  # returns [4, 9, 9]\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 0 ≤ length of `offsets` ≤ 10^5\n- -10^4 ≤ each offset ≤ 10^4\n",
